      "text": "To determine how many books Melvin left over after repacking them into boxes containing 40 books each, we start by calculating the total number of books and then find out how many full boxes of 40 books he can make.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of books:\n\\[\n\\text{Total number of books} = 1335 \\text{ boxes} \\times 39 \\text{ books/box} = 53065 \\text{ books}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find out how many full boxes of 40 books Melvin can make and how many books will be left over. We do this by dividing the total number of books by 40:\n\\[\n53065 \\div 40 = 1326 \\text{ R } 25\n\\]\nThis division tells us that Melvin can make 1326 full boxes of 40 books each, and there will be 25 books left over.\n\nThus, the number of books left over is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{25}\n\\]",
