      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine how many books are left over after unpacking all the books and repacking them into boxes of 40 books each, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of books in the warehouse.\n2. Determine how many full boxes of 40 books can be made from the total number of books.\n3. Find out how many books are left over after packing the full boxes.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of books in the warehouse:\n\\[\n1335 \\text{ boxes} \\times 39 \\text{ books per box} = 52065 \\text{ books}\n\\]\n\nNext, we determine how many full boxes of 40 books can be made from 52065 books:\n\\[\n52065 \\div 40 = 1301 \\text{ R } 25\n\\]\nThis division tells us that 1301 full boxes of 40 books each can be made, and there are 25 books left over. To see this more clearly, we can perform the division:\n\\[\n52065 \\div 40 = 1301 \\text{ R } 25\n\\]\nSo, the quotient is 1301 and the remainder is 25. Therefore, the number of books left over is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{25}\n\\]",
