      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine how many books are left over after Melvin repacks the books, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of books in the warehouse.\n2. Determine how many full boxes of 40 books can be made from the total number of books.\n3. Find out how many books are left over after repacking.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of books.**\n\nThere are 1335 boxes, and each box contains 39 books. Therefore, the total number of books is:\n\\[\n1335 \\times 39\n\\]\n\nTo perform the multiplication:\n\\[\n1335 \\times 39 = 1335 \\times (40 - 1) = 1335 \\times 40 - 1335 \\times 1\n\\]\n\\[\n1335 \\times 40 = 53400\n\\]\n\\[\n1335 \\times 1 = 1335\n\\]\n\\[\n53400 - 1335 = 52065\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 52065 books in total.\n\n**Step 2: Determine how many full boxes of 40 books can be made.**\n\nWe need to find out how many full boxes of 40 books can be made from 52065 books. This is done by dividing 52065 by 40:\n\\[\n52065 \\div 40 = 1301.625\n\\]\n\nThe integer part of the division gives us the number of full boxes:\n\\[\n1301\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Find out how many books are left over after repacking.**\n\nTo find the number of books left over, we calculate the remainder of the division:\n\\[\n52065 - (1301 \\times 40)\n\\]\n\\[\n1301 \\times 40 = 52040\n\\]\n\\[\n52065 - 52040 = 25\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of books left over is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{25}\n\\]",
